     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of amlodipine is 10 mg once daily. Usual doses are 2.5\u201310 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times the maximum. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and prolonged vasodilation, and it is in the range seen in overdoses. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who can review the patient's chart and take responsibility for the order.\n\n- **If 50 mg is a typo,** the prescriber should confirm the intended dose. For example, it may have been 5 mg. They can then place the order or ask me to enter it.\n- **If the dose really is intended,** the prescriber and a pharmacist should verify it directly before anything is ordered.\n\nIf you tell me the corrected dose, I can enter it once a prescriber has confirmed it."
      }
     ],
