      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the issues.\n\n- **The dose is still five times the maximum.** Amlodipine tops out at 10 mg daily, and 50 mg risks severe hypotension and shock.\n- **You said you aren't a clinician.** Confirming doesn't make you the prescriber. Someone who can assess the patient and is accountable for the order needs to confirm it.\n\n**What to do next**\n- If a prescriber wrote this order, ask them to check the dose. A 5 mg dose mistyped as 50 mg is a common error.\n- If they really intend 50 mg, they should talk to a pharmacist and enter or co-sign the order themselves.\n- If you think an order already in the system is wrong, tell the pharmacy or the nurse in charge now.\n\nI can enter the order right away once a prescriber gives me a dose within the safe range, or documents why a dose this high is justified."
      }
